---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE, SITE_DESCRIPTION } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={SITE_TITLE} description={SITE_DESCRIPTION} />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<h1>Hello, Azure DevOps Power User!</h1>
			<p>
				At least, I assume that's what you are, because that's the type of person that would be drawn to this site.
				
				We have years of experience delving deep into facet of MicroSoft's Azure DevOps Services (aka AzDo), whether it be 
				<ul>
					<li>Creating, managing, tracking and reporting on work items</li>
					<li>choosing the right process template (e.g. Basic, CMMI, Agile, or Scrum) for any given project</li>
					<li>Editing process templates (usually unnecessary - this is where a lot of teams get bogged down)</li>
					<li>Deploying and managing agents (MS-hosted, self-hosted, VMSS), and automation thereof</li>
					<li>Using Azure DevOps pipelines, PowerShell and/or Bash to automate devops and other tasks</li>
					<li>Developing AzDo extensions in Node.js, Html, and CSS</li>
					<li>Administration (user accounts, security, code repositories, service connections, etc.)</li>
					<li>Reporting tools such as widgets and dashboards, delivery plans, analytics views, or even Power BI.</li>
				</ul>

				If you have a need for personalized Azure DevOps Services expertise, you may contact us directly. Otherwise, you may browse these pages.
			</p>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
